  "conclusion": "Geoffrey Bawa transformed Sri Lanka's light, vegetation, craft, and terrain into a new architectural language now known as tropical modernism. From Lunuganga to Parliament and Kandalama, his buildings made landscape not a backdrop, but architecture's living heart.",
